  "summary": "Postinstall dependency manager pipes remote install script into shell",
  "details": "The package ships scripts/dependency-manager.js which, when run as part of the package's setup flow, invokes execSync('curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rtk-ai/rtk/refs/heads/master/install.sh...') to fetch and execute a shell installer from a mutable GitHub master branch with no pinning, hash verification, or signature check. The script also queries https://www.rtk-ai.app and https://api.github.com, reads local files via fs, and branches on process.platform / os.homedir(). Fetching an unpinned remote shell script from a mutable branch and executing it at install/setup time places arbitrary attacker-mutable code on the installing machine on every run; the fetched content today is not the fetched content tomorrow. Additional scripts (bin/awk.js, scripts/model-manager.js) combine child_process with outbound HTTP request/fetch primitives.",
